  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ta&apos;awon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is implemented in Palestine. The main outcome areas it contributes to are promoting peace and dialogue   mitigating armed conflict and social tensions. The rights holders and targeted actors are local civil society organisations, such as CBOs, local authorities and local public committees but also relevant national authorities that have a stake in conflict solution. Through building a database for conflict analysis, training actors (such as CBOs) to deal with conflict using evidence based methods and inclusive methods, and involving stakeholders in dialogue meetings, workshops and other fora, the project aims to achieve progressive development within the outcome areas.</narrative>
  </description>
